exports[`fscale facts > in a repo with projects in subfolders > prints the projects for people 1`] = `
"Package managers: npm, pip
Lockfiles: none
Languages: javascript, python, typescript
Tools: docker-compose, github-actions
Commands at the repo root:
  none
Projects (6):
  audit_service [python] backend/audit_service
    stack: python, pip, alembic, docker, pytest
    test: python -m pytest
    install: python -m pip install -r requirements-dev.txt
    interpreter: python (no virtual environment found, so python from the PATH: no .venv or venv folder in the project, no active VIRTUAL_ENV, and not a uv or poetry project)
  auth_service [python] backend/auth_service
    stack: python, pip, alembic, docker, pytest, ruff
    test: python -m pytest
    lint: python -m ruff check .
    install: python -m pip install -r requirements-dev.txt
    interpreter: python (no virtual environment found, so python from the PATH: no .venv or venv folder in the project, no active VIRTUAL_ENV, and not a uv or poetry project)
  frontend [node] frontend
    stack: javascript, typescript, npm, knip, oxlint, playwright, vite
    lockfiles: package-lock.json
    build: npm run build
    test: npm run test:run
    lint: npx --no oxlint
    typecheck: npx --no tsc --noEmit
    install: npm install
  ledger_service [python] backend/ledger_service
    stack: python, pip, alembic, docker, pytest
    test: python -m pytest
    install: python -m pip install -r requirements-dev.txt
    interpreter: python (no virtual environment found, so python from the PATH: no .venv or venv folder in the project, no active VIRTUAL_ENV, and not a uv or poetry project)
  market_service [python] backend/market_service
    stack: python, pip, alembic, docker, pytest
    test: python -m pytest
    install: python -m pip install -r requirements-dev.txt
    interpreter: python (no virtual environment found, so python from the PATH: no .venv or venv folder in the project, no active VIRTUAL_ENV, and not a uv or poetry project)
  realtime_service [python] backend/realtime_service
    stack: python, pip, alembic, docker, pytest
    test: python -m pytest
    install: python -m pip install -r requirements-dev.txt
    interpreter: python (no virtual environment found, so python from the PATH: no .venv or venv folder in the project, no active VIRTUAL_ENV, and not a uv or poetry project)
Graph (10 edges; fscale graph --explain says where each comes from):
  backend/audit_service -> .env.example (shared input)
  backend/auth_service -> .env.example (shared input)
  backend/auth_service -> backend/shared (Python import)
  backend/auth_service -> docker-compose.yml (shared input)
  backend/ledger_service -> .env.example (shared input)
  backend/ledger_service -> backend/shared (Python import)
  backend/market_service -> .env.example (shared input)
  backend/market_service -> backend/shared (Python import)
  backend/realtime_service -> .env.example (shared input)
  frontend -> .env.example (shared input)
Notes:
  frontend: the test script runs \`vitest\`, which watches for changes; verify uses test:run (\`vitest run\`) instead.
"
`;

